# Phase 6 - Advanced Search & Filtering
# Test File for REST Client (VS Code Extension)
# Install: REST Client by Huachao Mao

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api/v1
@token = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ====================================
### PUBLIC SEARCH ENDPOINTS
### ====================================

### 1. Basic Search - No Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/search
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. Search with Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=teff
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. Search with Multiple Filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=coffee&minPrice=100&maxPrice=500&minRating=4&sortBy=price_asc
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. Search with Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=teff&page=1&limit=5
Content-Type: application/json

### 5. Search by Location
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?location=Addis&sortBy=newest
Content-Type: application/json

### 6. Search by Category (Replace with actual UUID from your DB)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?categoryId=<your-category-uuid>&sortBy=rating
Content-Type: application/json

### 7. Autocomplete Suggestions
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/suggestions?query=te&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 8. Autocomplete with Short Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/suggestions?query=co
Content-Type: application/json

### 9. Get Popular Searches
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/popular?limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 10. Get Popular Searches (Top 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/popular?limit=5
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================
### AUTHENTICATION (Get Token First)
### ====================================

### Login as Customer
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer1@example.com",
  "password": "Customer123!"
}

### ====================================
### PROTECTED SEARCH ENDPOINTS
### ====================================

### 11. Get Recent Searches (Requires Auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/recent?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 12. Save a Search
# @name saveSearch
POST {{baseUrl}}/search/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Affordable Teff in Addis",
  "query": "teff",
  "filters": {
    "minPrice": 50,
    "maxPrice": 200,
    "location": "Addis Ababa",
    "minRating": 4
  },
  "notifyOnNewResults": true
}

### 13. Save Another Search
POST {{baseUrl}}/search/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Premium Coffee",
  "query": "coffee",
  "filters": {
    "minPrice": 200,
    "minRating": 4.5
  },
  "notifyOnNewResults": false
}

### 14. Get All Saved Searches
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 15. Get Specific Saved Search (Replace with actual ID)
@savedSearchId = {{saveSearch.response.body.data.savedSearch.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/{{savedSearchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 16. Update Saved Search
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/{{savedSearchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Search Name",
  "notifyOnNewResults": false
}

### 17. Update Saved Search Filters
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/{{savedSearchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filters": {
    "minPrice": 100,
    "maxPrice": 300
  }
}

### 18. Execute Saved Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/{{savedSearchId}}/execute?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 19. Execute Saved Search with Different Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/{{savedSearchId}}/execute?page=2&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 20. Delete Saved Search
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/{{savedSearchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================
### ERROR SCENARIOS
### ====================================

### 21. Invalid Price Range (minPrice > maxPrice)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?minPrice=500&maxPrice=100
Content-Type: application/json

### 22. Invalid Rating
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?minRating=6
Content-Type: application/json

### 23. Invalid Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?page=0
Content-Type: application/json

### 24. Invalid UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?categoryId=invalid-uuid
Content-Type: application/json

### 25. Query Too Short for Autocomplete
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/suggestions?query=a
Content-Type: application/json

### 26. Save Search Without Name
POST {{baseUrl}}/search/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "teff",
  "filters": {}
}

### 27. Save Search With Invalid Filters
POST {{baseUrl}}/search/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid Search",
  "filters": {
    "minPrice": 500,
    "maxPrice": 100
  }
}

### 28. Get Recent Searches Without Auth
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/recent
Content-Type: application/json

### 29. Save Search Without Auth
POST {{baseUrl}}/search/saved
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "filters": {}
}

### 30. Access Another User's Saved Search
# First create a search, then try to access it with a different user's token
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/saved/some-other-user-search-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================
### PERFORMANCE TESTS
### ====================================

### 31. Search with Max Limit
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?limit=100
Content-Type: application/json

### 32. Search with Complex Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=organic+premium+arabica+coffee&minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&minRating=4&location=Jimma&sortBy=relevance
Content-Type: application/json

### 33. Empty Search (List All)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?page=1&limit=20&sortBy=newest
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================
### EDGE CASES
### ====================================

### 34. Search with Special Characters
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=coffee%20%26%20tea
Content-Type: application/json

### 35. Search with Very Long Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=thisisaverylongquerytotesthowoursystemhandlesextremelylongse archstringsthatshouldnotbreakthesystem
Content-Type: application/json

### 36. Autocomplete with Numbers
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/suggestions?query=123
Content-Type: application/json

### 37. Zero Results Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=xyznonexistentproduct
Content-Type: application/json

### 38. Search by Exact Price
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?minPrice=100&maxPrice=100
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================
### SORTING TESTS
### ====================================

### 39. Sort by Price Ascending
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?sortBy=price_asc&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 40. Sort by Price Descending
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?sortBy=price_desc&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 41. Sort by Rating
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?sortBy=rating&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 42. Sort by Newest
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?sortBy=newest&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 43. Sort by Relevance with Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?query=teff&sortBy=relevance&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================
### NOTES
### ====================================

# To use this file:
# 1. Install "REST Client" extension in VS Code
# 2. Start your backend server: npm run dev
# 3. Click "Send Request" above each ### line
# 4. Variables like {{token}} are automatically extracted from responses
# 5. Replace <your-category-uuid> with actual UUIDs from your database
# 6. Tests #28-30 should fail (they test unauthorized access)
# 7. Tests #21-27 should return error responses (they test validation)
